The '''Daras national football team''' represents [[Daras]] in men's international association football. It is governed by the [[Daras Football Federation]] and is one of the more established teams in the [[AFA Men's World Ranking]], where it sits 20th in June 2026. The team is closely associated with [[Gongjing]], the capital, but draws talent from across the country's large industrial east, central heartland, and military-sporting system.

Daras are a technically disciplined and physically powerful side. Their football reflects the country's scale and centralised sporting structure: deep in squad depth, organised in possession, and difficult to unsettle in tournament play.

== History ==

=== Early development ===
Football in Daras developed in the late imperial and early republican periods around major urban centres such as [[Gongjing]], [[Xunyi]], and [[Luanjing]]. The sport first spread through universities, railway clubs, dockyards, and factory teams before becoming a major national pastime.

Unlike some smaller AFA states, Daras never relied on a single city or elite club system. Instead, football evolved through a broad, state-supported network of provincial teams and industrial clubs, which gave the national side a very wide player base. By the time the AFA tournament era matured, Daras had already become a familiar continental presence.

=== Socialist era ===
After the [[September Revolution]], football was reorganised under the socialist state. Youth academies, workplace sports associations, and provincial training centres became the backbone of the national game, producing highly disciplined players with strong tactical habits. The national team benefited from the same centralised planning that shaped Daras's wider economy and public institutions.

This system made Daras one of the most consistent sides in the AFA region, especially in tournaments where structure and squad cohesion mattered more than individual flair.

=== Modern era ===
In the modern era, Daras has remained a reliable continental contender. While it has not become one of the headline powers of the AFA the way [[Asikyira]], [[Balisca]], or [[Volisania]] have, it is respected as a difficult opponent with excellent physical conditioning and a deep bench of technically capable players. Its best World Cup run came in [[1986 AFA World Cup|1986]], when it reached the quarter-finals before losing to [[Burawa national football team|Burawa]].

Daras entered the [[2026 AFA World Cup]] in Group I alongside [[Burawa national football team|Burawa]] and [[Sinchew national football team|Sinchew]], placing it in one of the tournament's more competitive groups.

== Stadium ==

Daras play their home matches at [[Gongjing National Stadium]] in [[Gongjing]], the country's largest venue and symbolic centre of football culture. Important matches are also occasionally staged in [[Xunyi]] and [[Luanjing]].

== Playing style ==

The Darasian national team is generally described as a compact, technically organised side that combines possession football with strong defensive structure. The team tends to favour:

* controlled build-up play
* short passing through midfield
* disciplined defensive spacing
* strong set-piece execution
* high physical intensity and pressing

Daras's strongest teams have usually been those that blend the state's technical training systems with athletic, highly drilled defenders and midfielders. The result is a side that can dominate weaker opponents and remain competitive against stronger ones, even if it does not always play the most expansive football in the region.

